#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:172
msgid "Custom Git checkout commands (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:174
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports overriding the default :term:`checkout job <pre-"
"defined build jobs>` with a custom sequence of :program:`git` commands. "
"This is useful for advanced workflows like sparse checkouts or custom "
"cloning strategies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:178
msgid ""
"To enable this feature, go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings` "
"and update the :guilabel:`Git checkout command` field. Enter one command "
"per line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:184
msgid ""
"When you define custom Git checkout commands, Read the Docs will not run "
"the default Git clone or checkout. Your commands must perform the clone "
"and checkout of the desired revision."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:189
msgid ""
"If you just want to run some extra commands after the default Git "
"checkout, like unshallowing the clone or fetching extra branches, you "
"should use the ``build.jobs.post_checkout`` user-defined job instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:193
msgid ""
"In case you want to clone submodules, you can use the :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:submodules` config key for that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:196
msgid ""
"Commands are executed in order, in the repository working directory. You "
"can use :doc:`pre-defined environment variables </reference/environment-"
"variables>` such as :envvar:`READTHEDOCS_GIT_CLONE_URL`, "
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS_GIT_IDENTIFIER`, and "
":envvar:`READTHEDOCS_REPOSITORY_PATH`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:201
msgid "Example of custom Git checkout commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-customization.rst:211
msgid ""
